From c490087f0e0d6566891ed49bd9686f25a36c354d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcsm <mcsm@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:58:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] impeller (mcsm9): what S2's frame needs on Metal and
 Vulkan: R11G11B10 float, RGBA16 unorm, D16, D32 float, R32/RG32/RGBA32 uint,
 R16/RG16 float and RG32 float formats; 2x MSAA; 2D array and 3D textures
 (TextureDescriptor array_layer_count and depth; uploads per layer or depth
 slice; rendering into an array layer); depth-only render targets; storage
 images in compute passes; on Vulkan, compute passes move sampled and storage
 images to the layouts they read them in (and storage images back to
 shader-read after), compute writes are ordered before every later stage,
 depth targets that shaders sample end their pass shader-readable and read
 through a depth-only view, and pass boundaries order depth writes

